            <ArticleTitle>Takotsubo-like Myocardial Dysfunction in a Patient with Botulism.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2925-2927</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2169/internalmedicine.8968-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Botulinum toxin A (BTXA) can disrupt the neuromuscular and autonomic functions. We herein report a case of autonomic system dysfunction that manifested as Takotsubo-like myocardial dysfunction in a patient with botulism. Takotsubo syndrome results in acute cardiac insufficiency, another fatal complication of botulism in addition to respiratory muscle paralysis, particularly in patients with cardiovascular disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
